meta {
  name: 04 Update student
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/centers/me/students/{{studentId}}
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "firstName": "Awa-Marie",
    "phone": "+237690000001"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.firstName: eq Awa-Marie
}

docs {
  Edits a student, and moves them between tiers.

  ## Moving tier

  `{"tier": "PRO"}` is the most common thing a school does after buying: a
  Start student decides to sit the exam and needs Pro. The alternative was
  remove-and-re-add, which works but invites mistakes on an account holding
  the student's whole learning history.

  Allowed only into a tier with a FREE seat:

  - into a tier with room        -> 200, and `tier` in the response is the new
    one. The seat in the old tier is released by the same write, so that tier
    has room again immediately.
  - into a full tier             -> 403 SEAT_LIMIT_REACHED with the tier named
  - into a tier held at all      -> 403 TIER_NOT_HELD with the tier named
  - into the tier they ALREADY hold -> 200, even when that tier is exactly
    full. The student being moved does not count against their own
    destination, or a client re-sending the value it already has would be
    refused for no reason a user could understand.

  NO PRO-RATING. The move takes effect immediately for access; the price
  difference settles at the next renewal rather than being charged today. A
  school can move a student to Pro on day two and get Pro for most of a month
  at Start's price. That is accepted: the honest alternative is not "charge
  correctly", it is "build pro-rating", which is a project of its own.

  ## Concurrency

  Two administrators moving two different students into the LAST free Pro seat
  must leave exactly one of them in Pro. The check and the write share one
  Serializable transaction, so one of the two requests fails rather than both
  succeeding and putting the tier over its quantity.

  ## The allowlist

  All of these -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR:

  - `{"email": "attacker@example.com"}` — a center must not move an account's
    address
  - `{"password": "hunter2"}`
  - `{"centerId": "other-center"}`
  - `{"activatedAt": "2026-01-01"}`
  - `{"tier": "GOLD"}` or `{"tier": "pro"}`

  And `{}` -> 400 NO_STUDENT_FIELDS_SUPPLIED, before a transaction is opened.

  ## Scoping

  Another center's student id -> 404 STUDENT_NOT_FOUND, and the 404 comes
  BEFORE any seat is inspected. Answering "that tier is full" instead would
  confirm the id exists.

  A name change never touches seats: `{"firstName": "Awa-Marie"}` succeeds
  even when every tier is full, because nothing looks at a seat row unless a
  tier was supplied.
}
